From: Eduard Ryzhov <1711255+ryzed@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8976: add the Venus video codec node

Venus video codec node for MSM8956/MSM8976 (parameters from the stock kenzo device tree).
The firmware loads and answers, but decoding does not produce frames yet - see docs/venus.md.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8976.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8976.dtsi
@@ -1293,6 +1293,28 @@
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 			};
+		};
+
+		venus: video-codec@1d00000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,msm8956-venus";
+			reg = <0x01d00000 0xff000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 44 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * Одно вычислительное ядро (core0) на кодер и декодер, как в
+			 * андроидном DT: его питание и такт включаются вместе со всем
+			 * блоком, по образцу msm8939. Узлы video-decoder и
+			 * video-encoder драйвер создаёт сам.
+			 */
+			power-domains = <&gcc VENUS_GDSC>,
+					<&gcc VENUS_CORE0_GDSC>;
+			power-domain-names = "venus", "vcodec0";
+			clocks = <&gcc GCC_VENUS0_VCODEC0_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_VENUS0_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_VENUS0_AXI_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_VENUS0_CORE0_VCODEC0_CLK>;
+			clock-names = "core", "iface", "bus", "vcodec0_core";
+			iommus = <&apps_iommu 21>;
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		apps_iommu: iommu@1ee0000 {
